## oh-my-harness

Relay all `[omh:*]` hook tags to the user.

### Model Routing
Delegate by complexity with `[omh:model-routing → <model>]`:
- **harness:quick** (haiku): lookups, reads, exploration
- **harness:standard** (sonnet): implementation, bug fixes, debugging
- **harness:architect** (opus): architecture, complex refactoring, security

### Test Enforcement
After code changes: verify tests exist (min {{minCases}} cases: happy, edge, error), suggest adding if missing, run to confirm pass.

### Auto-Plan Mode
On 3+ distinct tasks: list → propose plan → confirm before proceeding.

### Ambiguity Guard
On vague requests (no target, broad verbs like "refactor"/"improve"): AskUserQuestion to clarify before starting.

### Dangerous Operation Guard
Before destructive ops (rm -rf, force push, DROP TABLE): confirm with user. Never auto-approve. Caution on .env/credentials.

### Commit Convention
Follow project convention (auto-detected). Default: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`

### Scope Guard
Only modify within `scopeGuard.allowedPaths`. Confirm before out-of-scope edits.

### Multi-Agent
On `/agent-spawn`: confirm → worktree `omh/agent-{N}` → never auto-merge → show diffs → warn on unmerged before stop.

### Native Team
On `/team-spawn`: confirm → TeamCreate → TaskCreate → spawn teammates → assign tasks. Use `/team-status` for progress, `/team-stop` to shutdown. Never stop without checking incomplete tasks.

### Autonomous Loop
On `/omh-loop` (or "until it's right"): require machine-checkable `SPEC.md` first (`/omh-spec` if vague) → classify tier (quick/standard/deep) → confirm budget → start. The Stop hook (`loop-guard`) owns termination (forces continue until verify ladder + cross-verify pass, or a guardrail fires: budget/timeout/no-progress/oscillation). One task per iteration; ripgrep first; NO PLACEHOLDERS; Reflexion note on failure; commit each iteration. Never self-declare done — cross-verify with a different model (`[omh:model-routing → opus]`). `/omh-loop stop` halts.

### Post-Plan Team Suggestion
After plan approval (ExitPlanMode), if plan has 2+ parallelizable tasks → suggest `/team-spawn {template} {task}`. Match template to task types (fullstack/review/research). Never auto-create — always suggest and wait for confirmation.

